":"oceanographic","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"relating to oceanography","word":"oceanográfico"}],"pos":"adj","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"Their lab is still analyzing the data from the last oceanographic survey.","bold_text_offsets":[[52,65]],"type":"example","id":"282bf7ef-a065-4fa9-b6c1-5ac263d91ce0"}],"links":[["oceanography","oceanography"],["ocean","ocean"]],"glosses":["relating to oceanography, the science of oceans"],"categories":["English adjectives","English entries with incorrect language header","English lemmas","English terms suffixed with -ic","English terms with usage examples","English uncomparable adjectives","Entries with translation boxes","Pages with 1 entry","Pages with entries","Terms with Catalan translations","Terms with Dutch translations","Terms with Esperanto translations","Terms with French translations","Terms with Galician translations","Terms with Irish translations","Terms with Italian translations","Terms with Norwegian Bokmål translations","Terms with Norwegian Nynorsk translations","Terms with Portuguese translations","Terms with Spanish translations"],"tags":["not-comparable"],"id":"3728c086-4f0a-41be-a2b8-901706117d61"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[{"word":"oceanographical"}]},"oceanic":{"id":"5df7ec86-945f-4cb2-8ff2-b771e3d13cf9","word":"oceanic","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"of or relating to the ocean","word":"oceânico"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"living in the ocean","word":"oceânico"}],"pos":"adj","tags":null,"senses":[{"links":[["ocean","ocean"]],"glosses":["Of or relating to the ocean."],"id":"91e4adba-28a6-4147-8e13-43c8825ba348"},{"examples":[{"text":"Nevertheless, the capacity of fleshy fruits to be dispersed by oceanic currents (resulting from their floatability and viability after prolonged exposure to saltwater) cannot be evaluated without empirical experimentation [3 ,7 ,10 ,16 ].","ref":"2015 October 15, “On the Limited Potential of Azorean Fleshy Fruits for Oceanic Dispersal”, in PLOS ONE, →DOI:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[63,70]],"id":"295988b4-21e1-4b04-a3d2-34812b477e99"}],"categories":["English terms with quotations"],"glosses":["Living in, produced by, or frequenting the ocean."],"id":"b1b32618-2f8c-4050-af38-63636765b564"},{"links":[["vastness","vastness"],["extent","extent"]],"glosses":["Resembling an ocean in vastness or extent."],"id":"6dd74876-c4a1-437f-b28c-6bc121ca14ab"},{"links":[["climate","climate"],["temperature","temperature"],["warmest","warmest"],["coldest","coldest"],["rainfall","rainfall"]],"glosses":["Having a climate that has a relatively small difference in temperature between the warmest and coldest times of the year, and relatively high rainfall"],"id":"6eb5fb15-d9d5-43d3-a6f3-b365315d883b"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"oceanian":{"id":"a969fb2c-77f2-4d84-9927-14ccc9a8ba87","word":"Oceanian","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"someone from Oceania","tags":["masculine"],"word":"oceânico"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"someone from Oceania","word":"oceaniense"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"links":[["Oceania","Oceania"]],"glosses":["Someone from Oceania (geographical region or continent)."],"id":"580823dd-4ca4-4830-8419-694d229136ea"},{"examples":[{"text":"In order to ensure that the Oceanians do get excited about Big Brother—displace, that is, eroticism from its natural object, another individual, to the State—the Party attempts in every way “to remove all pleasure from the sex act. . . . The only recognized purpose of marriage was to beget children for the service of the Party. Sexual intercourse was to be looked on as a slightly disgusting operation, like having an enema” (p. 57).","ref":"1986, Bernard Oldsey, Joseph Browne, editors, Critical Essays on George Orwell, G. K. Hall & Co., →ISBN, page 74:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[28,37]],"id":"29a69914-6172-4974-aaf3-2e6f87bdb23b"},{"text":"We might suppose that Orwell’s claims about the beliefs of Oceanians are simply implausible: after all, as the little thought experiment I started with demonstrates, we cannot just make ourselves believe on command.","ref":"2018, Iskra Fileva, “Bad Faith and Make-Believe”, in Ezio Di Nucci, Stefan Storrie, editors, 1984 and Philosophy: Is Resistance Futile? (Popular Culture and Philosophy; 116), Open Court Publishing Company, →ISBN:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[59,68]],"id":"23a5839b-dcf0-41c5-8f6f-af12d86c3dfc"},{"text":"Accordingly, the Ministry behaves in favor of the Party by making necessary amendments and manipulations in mass media to earn the sympathy of Oceanians.","ref":"2018, Murat Kalelioğlu, “Semiotic Analysis”, in A Literary Semiotics Approach to the Semantic Universe of George Orwell’s Nineteen Eighty-Four, Cambridge Scholars Publishing, →ISBN, section “George Orwell and “Nineteen Eighty-Four””, page 59:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[143,152]],"id":"a6da2c8f-1c9b-4f0c-8c0b-3185a16bcb14"}],"links":[["literary criticism","literary criticism"],["nation","nation"]],"categories":["English terms with quotations"],"raw_glosses":["(literary criticism) Someone from the fictional nation of Oceania in George Orwell’s novel Nineteen Eighty-Four (1949)."],"qualifier":"literary criticism","glosses":["Someone from the fictional nation of Oceania in George Orwell’s novel Nineteen Eighty-Four (1949)."],"id":"75c51362-eba5-4ccb-814a-4482970da447"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[{"word":"Oceanian","source":"Thesaurus:Oceanian"}]},"oceanarium":{"id":"a2da2c20-9807-43b5-876d-a7e8dbcab477","word":"oceanarium","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"park where visitors can see marine animals","tags":["masculine"],"word":"oceanário"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"links":[["park","park"],["marine","marine"],["mammal","mammal"],["fish","fish"]],"glosses":["A park wh